00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:47.870
On July 4, 1947, a strange craft crashed in the desert in New Mexico, America.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.220
What it was has yet to be proven.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.310
Conjecture has become fact, and rumor has become history.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.800
Who's there?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:07.180
In 1984, a manila envelope arrived at the home of TV producer Jaime Shandera.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:12.450
The envelope, from an anonymous source, contained a roll of undeveloped film.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.210
The film contained what is called the MJ-12 Document.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:28.900
Roscoe Hillenkoetter, head of the CIA at the time of the Roswell Incident,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.940
was at the top of the list of 12 members.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.910
It stated that these men concluded a secret treaty with extraterrestrials

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:38.740
as a special organization answerable only to the president.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.180
It is now accepted that President Truman's signature on the document

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:48.550
was in fact copied carefully from another document.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:55.360
Named as a member of MJ-12 was Vannevar Bush,

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.660
head of MIT's Department of Electrical Engineering.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.350
Connect to Wired.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:34.790
How could I turn something that did happen into something that didn't?

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.640
Are you Lain? I see, I see...

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.170
I don't know you.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.780
But you know me...

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.480
The flow of information doesn't always go both ways.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.840
Since the moment of the Wired's creation, you have always been here.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.430
Here, you are free.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.460
I'm trying to tell you that that's not me!

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.960
I suppose.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.670
How long have we been here, then?

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:13.030
At the very least, we cannot have been here since this world was created.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.160
That has nothing to do with it!

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.870
If a being is remembered, that proves that it's part of a record!

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.770
That's preposterous.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:29.050
How old do you think this "Lain" girl is? She's still a child!

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.820
Let's not worry about me now, okay? I...

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:54.950
The MEMEX memory expansion concept unveiled by Vannevar Bush in 1945

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.750
was a system whereby information recorded on microfilm

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.180
was projected onto a translucent screen.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:07.290
What he envisioned was the compression and rapid access of information.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.570
Even before the advent of computers,

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:15.200
Bush had already created the basis for our current multimedia

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.340
while he led the Manhattan Project atom bomb experiments.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.560
You forgot this.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.940
You forgot this on the floor here yesterday.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.630
If you don't need it, I'll toss it.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:55.200
I left that here?

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.200
That's what I'm sayin'.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.900
Conducting sensory deprivation experiments using

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:23.860
Native American narcotics and isolation tanks to probe the human unconscious,

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:29.510
John C. Lilly believed his experiments connected him to cosmic entities

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.530
by way of a communication network.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:37.180
Lilly dubbed the beings that guided him E.C.C.O.,

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.910
Earth Coincidence Control Office.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:51.990
Afterwards, Lilly began work on communication with dolphins.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.870
Dolphins are creatures which are able to conduct

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:01.140
wide-range networking in the water via ultrasonic waves.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.030
What?

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.370
You promised me earlier.

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.040
Promised what?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.460
That you'd go out with me.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.970
You said you'd go out with me!

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.400
W-What're you talking about?

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.670
Taro, is that true?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.910
Did I?

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.900
You didn't! You didn't!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:48.520
Even if I did, you aren't the you I want to go out with right now, Lain.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.490
Taro, you moron!

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:56.060
We're the same. I'm me. I'm the only me.

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:19.850
Awesome!

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.800
I can't believe you put together something like this!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:28.560
Oh, okay! This syncs up the parallel processors!

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:33.500
It's not pretty, but you can keep on expanding it this way.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:36.000
What're you using as coolant?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.870
Taro...

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.910
Is this liquid carbon?

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.150
Sit down over there.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.070
Damn...

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.410
I think you know what this is.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.050
It's you, isn't it, Taro?

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.550
You're with the Knights, aren't you?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:14.480
You're... the real Lain.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:20.980
I don't know whether or not there's another me in the Wired.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:26.810
But there's definitely no other me here in the real world.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:33.120
The other one with a body has only appeared in the club.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:38.160
You only need to manipulate the memories of the people there, right?

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.930
I... I can't...

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:54.210
Play track 44.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.310
It's almost over, isn't it?

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.730
Finally.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:17.630
So while we still can, we should...

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:45.990
Roger.

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:50.960
Now communicating.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.330
Stop.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.150
It's not me!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:22.050
But I knew the data coming into JJ's place had this kind of effect.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.970
If I had installed this chip, what would've happened to me?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:33.250
Would I have killed myself? Gone insane?

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.710
I said I don't know!

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:38.280
There's no way a kid like me could be a formal Knights member!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.220
I'm just a...

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:41.920
I wonder what this will do?

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:50.510
I-It's non-volatile memory! It'll overwrite existing memories!

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.590
What kind of memories?

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.760
I-I don't know.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:08.770
The Knights aren't just ordinary crackers, Lain.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:18.590
There's something strange about you. That's for sure.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:21.290
That's why the Knights are so interested.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:25.000
The Knights are users who are fighting

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.610
to make the only truth there is into a reality.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:34.910
I don't understand. What do you mean, "one truth"?

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.970
Like I said, I'm not a formal Knights member.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.270
They never explained it to me.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:45.610
But it's true. The truth has power because it's the truth.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:49.130
And because it's the truth, that makes it just.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:53.860
It's persuasive, isn't it? Don't you want truth like that?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.990
I'm going.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:03.600
Myu-Myu is jealous of you.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.400
Taro? Thank you.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:11.670
You...

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:28.690
Hey, this is a date, you know? I'm a guy. I had to do that.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:44.810
Ted Nelson, who studied under the two cult pioneers

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.040
Vannevar Bush and John C. Lilly,

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:53.020
proposed a giant electronic library in satellites in stationary orbit

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:58.890
which could be used at any terminal on Earth via radio or phone lines.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:04.520
He called this concept that would make this database "Xanadu."

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:14.170
The Mongolian utopia where all written cultures would never be lost.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.900
This was Xanadu.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:22.840
It was the concept of Hypertext that would make it real,

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:28.250
and Ted Nelson's name would go down in history as its originator.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:37.870
Hello, Navi.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:46.440
Click, click... Memory check...

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.670
Click, click...

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.540
Click, click...

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.790
That's... That's me?

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.870
Yes. This is me.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:51.390
Then who are they?

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:55.130
I'm you, so I wouldn't know.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.910
This is a lie.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:05.220
It's a lie. It's all a lie.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.780
Why are you doing this?

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:14.620
The Earth has its own specific electromagnetic waves.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:17.830
Between the ionosphere and the Earth's surface,

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:22.990
there is a constant resonance at a frequency of 8Hz in the ELF band.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:26.100
This is called the Schumann Resonance.

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:37.010
The extent of the effect on humans of these "Earth Brain Waves"

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:42.280
that the planet constantly gives off remains unknown.

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:46.330
The Earth's human population is approaching

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.060
the number of neurons in the brain.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:54.030
Douglas Rushkoff proposes that the consciousness of the Earth itself

00:19:54.030 --> 00:20:01.110
might be awakened when all humans on Earth become collectively networked.

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:09.140
The network's evolution would follow a neural model,

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:13.010
and just as neurons within the human brain are connected by synapses,

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:17.620
the Earth itself would become a neural network.

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:47.120
There is only one truth. God.

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:50.270
Yes. Me.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:56.030
Eiri Masami, Chief Researcher at Tachibana General Labs,

00:20:56.030 --> 00:21:00.590
further developed the hypothesis of a worldwide neural network.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:05.300
His hypothesis proposed a wireless network whereby all humanity

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:10.340
would be plugged in at an unconscious level without the need for any device.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:15.710
Furthermore, he encoded the Schumann Resonance Factor

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:20.310
and inserted it into the 7th-gen Wired Protocol on his own initiative.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:28.220
Upon discovering this, Tachibana General Labs dismissed Eiri.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:34.630
One week later, Eiri Masami's body was found on the Yamanote train line.

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:32.570
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:32.570
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:36.480
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:36.480
now I am punished.

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:42.780
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:42.780
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:49.690
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:49.690
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:00.880
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:00.880
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:05.330
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:05.330
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:11.520
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:11.520
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:18.760
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:18.760
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:26.810
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:26.810
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:36.720
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:36.720
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:42.330
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:42.330
You probably don't know

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:50.040
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:50.040
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
